Guard QPulseAudioContextManager::getContextState() against a null context.

m_context is reset to {} in three places: when pa_context_connect() fails, when the
server reports the context TERMINATED or FAILED, and in release(). Any contextIsGood()
call afterwards reaches pa_context_get_state(nullptr), which trips pa_assert(c) inside
libpulse and aborts the whole process — so a pipewire-pulse reconfiguration that
terminates the context takes down the next client to touch an audio sink.

QPulseAudioSink::validatePulseaudio() already handles a non-good context by warning and
setting QtAudio::Error::FatalError, so returning PA_CONTEXT_UNCONNECTED (not one of the
PA_CONTEXT_IS_GOOD states) simply lets that existing recovery path run.

--- a/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudio_contextmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudio_contextmanager.cpp
@@ -598,6 +598,8 @@
 pa_context_state_t QPulseAudioContextManager::getContextState()
 {
     auto lock = std::lock_guard{ *this };
+    if (!m_context)
+        return PA_CONTEXT_UNCONNECTED;
     return pa_context_get_state(m_context.get());
 }
